abstract: >-
  Quantum Spectrodynamics (QSD) derives the gauge couplings,
  particle masses, and cosmological constant of the Standard Model
  from the algebraic geometry of the [[5,1,3]] quantum error-correcting
  code, requiring zero free parameters beyond the Planck mass. The
  framework introduces three fundamental constants — the holographic
  bit density Hb_4 = 1/(4 ln 2), geometric strain sigma = 3/(80 phi^2),
  and spectral bond varpi = pi*phi^2 — from which all Standard Model
  parameters are derived through topological renormalization on the
  K4-C5 graph structure. Predictions agree with experiment to within
  0.002%-1.2% across six independent observables.
